<http://data.silknow.org/object/7123c145-1a1c-300b-a7e3-81787375552c>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Panel of painted silk, China, ca. 1820-1840"@en , "Panel of pale blue tabby plain-weave silk with yellow selvedges. Painted with tiny sprays of flowers, some tied with a ribbon, in orange, red, purple, pink, white, lilac, and three shades of green. The silk is pinned at the selvedges and across the material. Two ends are hemmed."@en , "This silk was painted in China for export to Europe. These floral textiles were popular in the West from the end of the 18th century until about 1900. They were made up into women's dresses and also used for furnishings. This type of fabric was not used in China itself."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/9c375479-9d53-3cd5-abab-558016f14a2a> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Panel of pale blue tabby plain-weave silk with yellow selvedges. Painted with tiny sprays of flowers, some tied with a ribbon, in orange, red, purple, pink, white, lilac, and three shades of green. The silk is pinned at the selvedges and across the material. Two ends are hemmed."@en , "Panel of painted silk, China, ca. 1820-1840"@en , "This silk was painted in China for export to Europe. These floral textiles were popular in the West from the end of the 18th century until about 1900. They were made up into women's dresses and also used for furnishings. This type of fabric was not used in China itself."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/7123c145-1a1c-300b-a7e3-81787375552c/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/7123c145-1a1c-300b-a7e3-81787375552c/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/7123c145-1a1c-300b-a7e3-81787375552c/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/7123c145-1a1c-300b-a7e3-81787375552c/dimension/1> ;
